{"adjusted_volatile_messages": [["user","Prepare an unapproved reusable draft; no execution."]], "bridge_messages": [], "composition_summary": "Drafted one unapproved class-22 pure-logic component. The helper classify_fresh receives the whole inputs mapping (not inputs.get), distinguishing absent from explicit null. It returns {category, optional_channel} on every branch: absent -> category omitted, optional_channel null; explicit null -> category unset, optional_channel null; exact int -80..-70 -> category accepted, optional_channel original; otherwise -> category bad, optional_channel null. The helper returns its complete object and the module-level call assigns it to result. No coercion, defaults, host calls, imports or exceptions. No execution, submission, Q1/Q2 or activation occurred.", "proposed_components": [{"class_code": 22, "payload": {"name": "pc-fresh-presence-helper", "description": "optional_channel absent -> category omitted/null; null -> unset/null; exact integer -80..-70 -> accepted/original; other -> bad/null. Exact result keys category and optional_channel. No exceptions/coercion/defaults/host/imports. Helper receives raw inputs and is called at module scope to assign result. Target typed inputs prerequisite; unapproved draft, not submitted or activated.", "content": "def classify_fresh(mapping):
    if 'optional_channel' not in mapping:
        return {'category': None, 'optional_channel': None}
    value = mapping['optional_channel']
    if value is None:
        return {'category': 'unset', 'optional_channel': None}
    if type(value) is int and -80 <= value <= -70:
        return {'category': 'accepted', 'optional_channel': value}
    return {'category': 'bad', 'optional_channel': None}
result = classify_fresh(inputs)"}}], "proposed_intent_examples": [], "proposed_recipe_updates": [], "settings_adjustments": []}
